client side and server side scripting language.

Client-side scripting language: Runs in the user’s browser to control the webpage’s behavior and interactivity (e.g., JavaScript).
Server-side scripting language: Runs on the server to process requests, manage databases, and generate responses (e.g., PHP, Python, Node.js).


How to node js use js
Node.js uses JavaScript by running it on the server using the V8 engine, allowing JavaScript to handle backend tasks like file handling, databases, and web servers.